  "description": "LUYCUE crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C86 H111 Lu3 N2 O15 S8,4.5(C3 H7 N1 O1),3.5(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Lu1 (Lu) has 7 O neighbors; Lu2 (Lu) has 6 O neighbors; Lu3 (Lu) has 7 O neighbors; Lu4 (Lu) has 7 O neighbors; Lu5 (Lu) has 6 O neighbors; Lu6 (Lu) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.413-3.431 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 94.30-99.07°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C86H111Lu3N2O15S8·4.5(dmf)·3.5(H2O) (crystal C99.5H149.5Lu3N6.5O23S8). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
